es are 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham and Norvane together are about 56% of those utility orders, so they drive most of the demand.\n  - Funding is a risk. Debt markets are open, but bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Equity markets look unreliable. If Pellham can't fund its plan, equipment orders could slip. I did not check the funding evidence myself. It comes from n3's work and its sub-nodes.\n- **Data centres (secondary, slowing):**\n  - Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026 because power availability limits new sites.\n  - Connection requests are only a proxy for equipment orders. I found no direct order data and no 2026 growth figure, so I can't say how big the slowdown is.\n- **Limits:** I found no backlog or order data for 2027. Nothing confirms that the plans will turn into orders.\n\nDetail is in n7.r1 (utilities) and n8.r1 (data centres).","ttft_ms":2255,"type":"result","duration_ms":35758,"uuid":"6d459b21-513b-4c90-a3b6-61dc9fe66ce5","ttft_stream_ms":1003,"time_to_request_ms":134,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":11,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":14,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":19,"query_setup":3,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":6,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":80,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":63,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":194,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":120,"process_rss_mib_result":200,"process_anon_mib_result":118,"process_peak_rss_mib":202,"process_cpu_ms_turn":601,"process_wall_ms_turn":35755,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":78,"process_wall_ms_streaming":2710,"main_stream_count":3,"main_strea